  "id": "COMPOUND:25671 - PROTEIN:5999",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 3'-O-Methyltricetin may act as a target for multiple downstream pathways leading to the activation of Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. This is supported by the fact that 3'-O-Methyltricetin is linked to Inosine-5'-monophosphate dehydrogenase 1, which is a target of a compound that ultimately affects the expression of the gene in macrophages. Additionally, 3'-O-Methyltricetin is also linked to Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits, which are targets of other compounds, and both of these pathways are associated with the expression of the same gene in macrophages. The integration of these pathways suggests that 3'-O-Methyltricetin may influence macrophage function through multiple mechanisms, potentially modulating gene expression in a complex and interconnected manner. The evidence highlights the importance of targeting these pathways to achieve the desired effect on macrophage gene expression.",
